Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.72,0:00:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where did I put it...?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.05,0:00:08.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know it's in here somewhere...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.45,0:00:10.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh...?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.48,0:00:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.92,0:03:41.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.08,0:03:45.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.11,0:04:07.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.81,0:04:18.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this? Something Indian?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.20,0:04:22.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two are going home, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.99,0:04:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.38,0:04:28.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, would you let me lend you a hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.21,0:04:31.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know I can be of some help to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.43,0:04:35.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, we'd love that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.81,0:04:38.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.97,0:04:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...says that about 2,000 years\Nhas passed, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.43,0:04:45.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and what happened\Nto that cool ship you had?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.48,0:04:49.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, now... We'll have\Nplenty of time for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.83,0:04:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll tell you all about it on the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.21,0:04:53.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay...\NHuh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\bord0\blur1\c&H434545&\fnCaveat Brush\pos(737.332,730.668)}Final draft! Project Robinson Ver 3.0\NNagara, did you put all this\Ntogether?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.73,0:04:59.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.14,0:05:02.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, if we take this... and do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.83,0:05:04.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,800)}There, it's perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.10,0:06:06.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.92,0:06:08.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pretty handy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.76,0:06:15.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, that is awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.76,0:06:15.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Awesome! Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.97,0:06:20.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay,\Nwe're good here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.76,0:06:24.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.91,0:06:27.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you take it from here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.07,0:06:30.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.45,0:06:39.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mizuho.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.96,0:06:45.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not going to use that over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.03,0:06:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nah, I can do what\NI need from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.20,0:06:49.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.53,0:06:52.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as long as I'm doing this,\NI want to watch it with my own eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.00,0:06:57.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So you really aren't going\Nto come home with us, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.13,0:07:00.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm. I'm staying here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.57,0:07:10.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani, didn't you ever feel homesick?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.70,0:07:13.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were all by yourself\Nfor 2,000 years, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.58,0:07:16.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homesick... now there's\Na sensation that takes me back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.63,0:07:22.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was a world that I stopped by before\Nthat painted really close pictures\Nof scenes from my old home.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.71,0:07:27.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were shockingly accurate and vivid,\Nbut most of all, mysterious.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.55,0:07:30.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So much so that they made me feel uneasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.04,0:07:35.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was the first time since we went\Nadrift that I felt any sense of nostalgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.50,0:07:39.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I decided to call that\N{\i1}This {\i0}World "Homesick."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.78,0:07:43.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By "old home," do you mean\Nthe world we came from?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.78,0:07:46.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but also, kind of different.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.92,0:07:50.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The world was more "our-world-like"\Nthan it was "our world."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.93,0:07:55.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The master of that world was almost\Npathologically caught up in his memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.18,0:07:57.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and kept recreating his homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.17,0:08:02.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The strange thing was,\Nno matter how far you went in this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.17,0:08:04.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there was never another soul\Nrepresented anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.83,0:08:07.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds like a lonely place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.55,0:08:12.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, when a certain time approached,\Nthe style radically changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.08,0:08:14.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I saw those images,\NI was taken aback.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.68,0:08:17.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were the likeness\Nof this one female student.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.75,0:08:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was depicted as\Na real beauty, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.18,0:08:23.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, this girl\Nused to be his girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.35,0:08:26.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is starting to get interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.39,0:08:27.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.68,0:08:29.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I gave in to my curiosity, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.93,0:08:35.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I took a look at her with my Scoop Scope,\Na power holdover that I developed myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.87,0:08:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and...?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.15,0:08:40.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The actual girl was not\Nnearly as pretty as her image.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.13,0:08:44.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those love goggles come\Nwith a strong prescription.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.81,0:08:48.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, the girl really did love him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.78,0:08:52.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It got me curious,\Nso I peered into the other images.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.55,0:08:57.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His actual home was a town that I knew,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.55,0:08:59.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which wasn't as beautiful or nearly\Nas attractive as how he had depicted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.36,0:09:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Put simply, he didn't accept reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.61,0:09:10.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His girlfriend wanted him to live\Nin the reality in front of his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.18,0:09:12.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he refused to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.43,0:09:17.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So eventually, she got fed up with him,\Nand she left that world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.56,0:09:22.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then he began painting pictures\Nof his girlfriend like a man possessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.93,0:09:26.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That figure of her was\Nwhat was in the paintings.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.73,0:09:29.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It felt as though I had been\Nunexpectedly confronted by reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.68,0:09:33.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought, can I say I'm actually\Nliving my own life in reality?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.12,0:09:41.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She didn't want to create\Nbeautiful memories with him;
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.23,0:09:45.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she wanted to create a future\Nwith him that was still unformed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.85,0:09:52.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At some point, he became\Na captive to his memories of her,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.83,0:09:55.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that became his entire world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.58,0:09:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did he die?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.58,0:09:59.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, I'm not sure\Nexactly how to answer that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.05,0:10:02.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Death in {\i1}This {\i0}World is\Na little bit complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.52,0:10:09.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I think about dying,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.58,0:10:12.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's dark, and scary,\Nand makes my chest feel tight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.09,0:10:16.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that's how\Nit was for Nozomi, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.53,0:10:18.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did she feel afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.55,0:10:35.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara,\Nhave you been to see\Nthe world where Nozomi died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.69,0:10:37.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.03,0:10:39.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then how were you able\Nto make certain that she died?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.19,0:10:45.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. Mizuho's cat, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.09,0:10:50.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She is able to tell...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.87,0:10:53.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...the status of {\i1}all {\i0}things.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.68,0:10:58.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was an inventor in one world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.48,0:11:04.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The students who were in that world\Nbelieved themselves to\Nbe the children of God,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.53,0:11:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and were convinced that they had\Nto keep their minds and bodies spotless.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.97,0:11:14.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They made up their minds\Nto live without killing,\Nwithout eating meat,\Nand to not even kill any plants.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.16,0:11:17.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a world of fasting.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.68,0:11:20.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds like an awfully difficult world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.65,0:11:24.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, actually, they seemed\Nsurprisingly happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.58,0:11:28.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That world flourished with a beautiful,\Nadvanced civilization,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.53,0:11:30.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and had a lot of\Nholdovers remaining in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.63,0:11:33.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, you don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.38,0:11:38.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For one thing,\Nhunger isn't that big a deal to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.44,0:11:45.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the fringe of that world,\Nthere was a student who\Nwas obsessed with dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.95,0:11:50.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was trying to produce\Ndeath here in this static world—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.33,0:11:51.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,an inventor of "death."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.38,0:11:53.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Invent "death"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.11,0:11:55.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.13,0:11:59.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was trying to upset the stasis\Nof this world through people's deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.10,0:12:03.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To tell you the truth,\NI kind of admired him a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.39,0:12:08.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His sense of morals aside, this was\Na challenge directed at {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.23,0:12:11.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.70,0:12:15.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...the actual guy was the devil himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.13,0:12:17.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He reviled God, burned down the forests,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.98,0:12:21.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,wolfed down meat, and held\Nthose who fasted in contempt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.93,0:12:26.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, he took\Nadvantage of the stasis here\Nto conduct experiments in suicide\Nand murder over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.21,0:12:29.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This guy sounds like\Nnothing more than a serial killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.92,0:12:32.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.08,0:12:37.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was so utterly atrocious,\NI honestly felt like killing him myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.86,0:12:41.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, finally, he invented "death."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.83,0:12:46.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He... apparently wanted to die so badly,\Nhe couldn't help himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.03,0:12:48.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So he was the very first person\Nhe used his invention on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.63,0:12:51.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he died with flying colors.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.19,0:12:52.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.73,0:12:54.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.67,0:12:57.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I actually found his invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.13,0:13:03.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was like...\N...he was telling me to have a seat, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.13,0:13:07.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Did you sit down?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.67,0:13:15.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He didn't look at all different\Nfrom who he was before he died.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.52,0:13:19.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But with each passing day,\Nthe changes began appearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.34,0:13:22.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The inventor no longer had any desires.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.04,0:13:27.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He accepted what he saw in\Nfront of him, was content with it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.18,0:13:30.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and no longer offered any\Ncriticism or hatred of anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.78,0:13:33.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He became a well-adjusted person,\Nnot unlike a Buddha.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.96,0:13:37.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The inventor had left {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.69,0:13:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He knew that when\Nhis drive came to an end,\Nit marked the end of his life as he was.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.13,0:13:48.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is one form of "death" in {\i1}This {\i0}World.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.92,0:13:52.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I ended up not sitting down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.47,0:13:55.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you suppose he hated himself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.09,0:13:57.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.23,0:14:02.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all this time,\NI don't know why he was\Nso obsessed with dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.73,0:14:05.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But after living for so long,\NI understand something—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.73,0:14:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as you keep building up all sorts of\Nexperiences and what have you,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.88,0:14:11.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's something about you\Nthat grows more and more irregular.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.01,0:14:16.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The larger it gets, the more\Nindividual meanings become diluted,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.73,0:14:19.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the more homogenized\Nthings become, I'd say.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.13,0:14:23.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can tell that I'm steadily growing more\Napathetic the more unbalanced I get.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.68,0:14:26.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ultimately, I'll end up as\Na gaping, lopsided hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.77,0:14:35.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm being drained away by time,\Nuntil someday, I'll become\Na mere shape, much like Nozomi has.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.03,0:14:38.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's nothing more than another\Nstate incorporated into this stasis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.53,0:14:40.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that can be called "death," then...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.88,0:14:43.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...it's no different than\Nthe "death" in our own world.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.63,0:14:48.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. There's no such thing as a soul,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.48,0:14:51.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and our consciousness is born\Nfor no reason, then it just fades away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.66,0:14:54.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Life is an endless\Nexercise in vain effort.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.19,0:15:00.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's precisely\Nbecause it's meaningless
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.43,0:15:04.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that I think the brilliance of\Nthis moment in life is so precious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.50,0:15:08.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because that one moment\Nbelongs to that person alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.08,0:15:11.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nozomi isn't ever coming back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.69,0:15:15.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.15,0:15:28.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...her will still lives on.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.93,0:15:33.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How much of it is finished?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.98,0:15:38.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cats are doing their best,\Nbut I'd have to say about 20%.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.78,0:15:41.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did try reaching out to the others...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.73,0:15:45.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...but they all said\Nthey weren't going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.60,0:15:48.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It ended up being just\NMizuho and me... and...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.42,0:15:51.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...Nozomi who were going.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.05,0:15:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doing it like this means that\Nin going back to our own world,\Nwe might end up not\Nbeing who we are anymore,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.09,0:15:59.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.53,0:16:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.48,0:16:06.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Plus the time it will take.\NEven if we do make it back, two years\Nwill have passed since we went adrift.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.23,0:16:09.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And there's a chance\Nthat I'll be dead there.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.93,0:16:11.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.10,0:16:15.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, there's no use in thinking\Nabout what might happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.73,0:16:17.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I could just as well be alive, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.70,0:16:22.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everything that took place here\Ncould end up as though it never happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.68,0:16:23.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if it does...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.19,0:16:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm?\NNever mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.07,0:16:29.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me, if we do get back...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.86,0:16:32.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...what's the first thing you want to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.98,0:16:35.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I haven't given that any thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.63,0:16:37.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not? It's fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.40,0:16:41.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I mean, we might not\Neven remember any of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.78,0:16:44.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And there's no use in thinking\Nabout what might happen, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.73,0:16:48.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Then, are you calling me\Na fool for thinking so much about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.18,0:16:50.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm just saying, it's not a big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.76,0:16:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hm-hmm, you know what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.03,0:16:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to have a Soleil omu-rice,\Nsomething with a ton\Nof grace strawberries on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.53,0:17:01.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then eat my fill of\NChinese noodles from Hatsune...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.43,0:17:02.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see? I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.20,0:17:05.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a bunch of nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.47,0:17:12.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that,\NI'm going to find the\Ncurmudgeonly-looking boy\Nfrom the corner of the staff room,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.83,0:17:15.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,grab him by the scruff of the neck,\Nand ask him a question.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.86,0:17:19.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.84,0:17:24.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Will you be my friend once again?"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.18,0:17:29.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once I do, what do you\Nsuppose he will answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.62,0:17:33.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're already high-schoolers.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.90,0:17:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.91,0:17:37.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.58,0:17:38.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.19,0:17:39.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.66,0:17:44.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...you and me being friends\Nwill have never happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.66,0:17:48.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have torn up your textbook again,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.53,0:17:50.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and I'll have abandoned that bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.12,0:17:53.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.98,0:17:56.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've made\Na lot of progress since then.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.51,0:18:01.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no telling\Nif what happened here...\N...will still have\Nhappened over there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.15,0:18:07.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still,\Nthey {\i1}did {\i0}for sure happen here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.94,0:18:12.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, how about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.60,0:18:14.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whichever one of us\Nremembers has to do as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.42,0:18:19.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to become friends again.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.33,0:18:22.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay? Promise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.45,0:18:25.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Promise me you won't refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.13,0:18:30.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.16,0:18:40.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how well I've come to understand\Nthe psychology of this universe, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.48,0:18:46.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...can't do anything more for a friend\Nwho's crying but sit next to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.44,0:18:57.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you...!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.20,0:19:04.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rajdhani...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.10,0:19:07.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need to ask you about something.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.03,0:19:07.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.94,0:19:12.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's one item I want\Nto add to Project Robinson.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.40,0:19:16.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, now we're talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.08,0:19:21.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know we can't change the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.63,0:19:23.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.76,0:19:33.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, analog-style.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.07,0:19:36.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Heh-heh, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.85,0:19:40.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the very same rocket that\Nfirst took mankind to the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.83,0:19:41.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's good luck, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.60,0:19:45.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cat's copies are\Naccurately reproduced.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.57,0:19:48.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what's up top is even more primitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.49,0:19:50.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mizuho,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.12,0:19:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why did you want to go home?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.50,0:19:56.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because I... have things I want to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.08,0:19:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cats can't live over there anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.73,0:20:04.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.56,0:20:09.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Actually, it's pretty easy to\Nget back to our own world.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.36,0:20:13.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But to do so requires\Nresolve and sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.51,0:20:16.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't get back\Nthe time that has passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.02,0:20:19.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you two can still make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.36,0:20:23.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, we're not simply\Ngoing back, are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.91,0:20:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right. Nagara is...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.81,0:20:28.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry I'm late.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.83,0:20:31.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now everything is ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.11,0:20:34.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow is the big day.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.91,0:20:40.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough already.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.40,0:20:42.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm staying here with the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.21,0:20:47.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you ever happen to run into me,\Nit would be my pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.59,0:20:50.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.61,0:20:53.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.39,0:20:55.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'll take care of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.95,0:20:58.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks for everything you've done.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.46,0:21:03.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yamabiko, you take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.61,0:21:09.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sakura! See you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.49,0:21:12.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have to go now!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.63,0:21:17.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.61,0:21:19.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...left my cats behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.16,0:21:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure the cats feel the same as we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.02,0:21:31.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if Sakura will\Nwatch over them, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.17,0:21:32.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.83,0:21:38.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fifteen seconds to launch.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.18,0:21:39.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Switching to internal power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.66,0:21:41.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Twelve...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.70,0:21:42.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...eleven...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.77,0:21:43.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,ten...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.94,0:21:44.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...nine...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.94,0:21:47.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ignition start.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.53,0:22:15.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Launch pad safely cleared\Nand you are on course.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.47,0:22:18.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all the support I can give you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.91,0:22:20.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good luck to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.14,0:22:22.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Copy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.48,0:22:24.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Farewell, Rajdhani.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.45,0:22:33.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm, now then...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.63,0:22:37.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.80,0:22:39.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...must be from Mizuho.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.23,0:22:40.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, this...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.47,0:22:48.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing matters in {\i1}This {\i0}World...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.75,0:22:51.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...but once in a while,\Ncool things do happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.47,0:22:54.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is why I can get by.
